   102	
   103	He had learned. That was what made him the best the cohort had built. In the third exchange he did not stamp to his own count any more.
   104	
   105	He stamped faster, shorter, left and right and centre as he came, two counts apart instead of four, none of them as hard as before but each one coming before the last had lain down, so that the boards a stride ahead of him were jumping across the whole width of his reach. He came on behind them. Within a dozen heartbeats there was no still wood between Lira and him anywhere she could reach in a step.
