   109	She tried the four-count once, and the lie on the second count put her front foot on boards that had been still a moment earlier and were jumping now, and her foot went sideways, and she went with it. She did not burst. She scrambled, two ugly running steps and a hop, out of the jumping boards on her own legs, and came up near the east wall beside the striking frames on their thick springs. He came after her. Not fast; Force fighters were never fast. Stamp, settle, step, stamp, a stride at a time, the floor ahead of him jumping like water coming up a beach.
