   172	
   173	A skein of geese went over, very high, calling.
   174	
   175	Cael counted the cut out of the window as they went, because he counted everything. Four hundred and forty yards, near enough, by the coachman's pace and the bends at each end. At the far end, the east end, the road narrowed to cross a culvert where a stream came down a gully off the hill and went under the road toward the river, with a low stone parapet on either side. Beside the near parapet stood a milestone. He could not read it from that distance. It would say seven.
   176	
   177	Across the road just short of the culvert stood a cart.
   178	
   179	It was an ordinary farm cart with its shafts down on the road and no horse in them, slewed across the crown so that it blocked most of the way. One of its wheels was off and lying flat beside it. There was nobody near it.
   180	
