+# Book 6 — *The Compact's Hand*: line and listening proof notes
+
+Reader: Codex, independent fresh-context review seat. Date: 2026-10-11. No manuscript file modified; no git command run.
+
+## Read-before-manuscript record
+
+- Read Book 4 and Book 5 `listening-proof.md` in full and carried their proof structure and standards.
+- Read `COMPLETION-PLAN.md`, `whole-arc-read.md`, `LANE-RULINGS.md`, `PASS-BRIEF.md`, both lane reports, `EDITION_BRIEF.md`, `OWNER-DECISIONS.md` through #50 (especially #3, #11, #33, #35–#47), BOOK_MAP §8, all of `protected-patterns.txt`, and `audio/fpaudio.py`.
+- Read the Book 1 and Book 3 pronunciation tables, plus Book 4 and Book 5's tables, for shared entries.
+- Owner constraints carried: Cael = KAYL; Lira = LEER-a; Bede/Maud/Gwen/Abbot are placeholders, not findings; no season names or month order; Halcenvane weekdays First-day … Seventh-day; feet/yards; Book 5 ratings and bout formats; Book 6 calendar; ch49's protected certification minute remains the form's own mislabel (#47).
+- Protected text: no proposed change may touch BOOK_MAP §8, the 51 protected patterns, either FRAGMENT ACQUIRED notice, or the protected closing inventory/exchange added by #46.
+
+## Mechanical sweep before the read
+
+- Scope: 60 files, 294,099 `wc` words. Aggregate content hash before proof: `4419e7130cb76fe550fe334507e2479b6373528047f83f514cb44fda2f4bb00f` (filename plus bytes in chapter order).
+- 254 `---` breaks; all have a blank line before and after.
+- Three fenced blocks (six fence lines): ch32 Anchor notice, ch37 first stability warning, ch54 Blade notice. No underscores, strikethrough or curly quotes. Backticks occur only in those fences. Asterisks balance in every paragraph.
+- Eight odd-quote paragraphs: ch35:259–263 (one multi-paragraph quoted letter), ch51:177 (multi-paragraph reading of the ruling), ch52:215–221 (Karis's multi-paragraph forfeiture list). Verify endings and voice continuity in place.
+- One pre-existing trailing space: ch17:185, already reported by Lane A. No tabs or doubled spaces.
+- Apparent non-terminal paragraphs to verify in place: ch14:112 (struck-through unfinished half-line ending `by`); ch47:251 (`In the records hall`).
+- Repeated-word sweep found only grammatical `had had` (18 hits across 15 chapters).
+- 106 flattened paragraphs exceed 700 characters; list only in the final proof.
+- Early engine-risk candidate: ch16:161 italic figure `0` (likely `nought`, subject to full-context read and protection check).
+
+## Chapter read notes
+
+### Ch1–5
+
+- Ch1: clean. Log paragraphs flatten intelligibly; `Wind` always the Path/noun. The `bow` in “drawn bow” is BOH. Multi-person hall scene tags and alternation hold. No join damage.
+- Ch2: clean. Lira/Stone/Rooke floor speech is attributable; Karis/assistant sequence is clear. Rating explanation agrees with #38. `Mm.` is Seln's load-bearing answer and needs render checking.
+- Ch3: clean. Bracken/Brom share the refectory scene but remain distinct by role and sound. Wing-three calls are flat and attributable. `lead` in “lead hand” = LEED; no competing LED in scene.
+- Ch4: clean. Three-person night-floor runs are carried by content and physical positions. The lane bill is ten counts, clean at eleven. No lost tag after Lane A cuts.
+- Ch5: clean. The challenge's first page is italic document voice; `[SHATTERED]` brackets silent. Withrow's document reading and subsequent speech remain distinct. Protected “season's open” is generic season usage, not a season name.
+
+### Ch6–13
+
