    34	
    35	"In the matter of Caelen Hesk-ward," said the seat's clerk. "Upon the close. The twelfth sitting. The petitioner."
    36	
    37	Jent rose.
    38	
    39	He had no folder today. He had left even the one folder on the table, shut, with his spectacles lying on it, and he stood in front of the platform with his hands at his sides, as a man stands who has come to say a thing he could say in his sleep and does not wish to seem to be reading it.
    40	
    41	"The seat allowed each party an hour," he said. "The petitioner will use ten minutes, and I should like to say why, so that it is not taken for discourtesy. There is very little left between the parties. I have spent a year making sure of that."
    42	
