editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-12.md:5:Nobody had announced the trial beyond a line on Rooke's own board, chalked the evening before in his square capitals: *PROGRAM TRIAL. SECOND-DAY, SECOND BELL. LIRA / FORCE THIRD-YEAR. RATED.* But the house had read it, and the house knew what *rated* meant on that floor. It meant the first bout ever fought on the program's painted boards under the program's own seal, with a figure at the end of it that would go into the program's own book. By the half-bell the gallery was full along both sides. By the second bell the porters had opened the shutters on the high windows to let the heat out, and the light came down onto the white crosses in long bright bars, and there were people standing on the gallery stair.
