editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-20.md:5:They went in at the quarter to the eleventh bell, as they always did, on the key Rooke had lent Lira for the program's dawn drills and had told her he did not want to know about after dark. But the east hall was not what it had been. The shutters along the gallery had been closed since the Fourth-day by Rooke's order, and they did not need to be drawn. The chain still hung across the foot of the gallery stair with its padlock and its card, *CLOSED TO OBSERVERS*, so that Brom had to step over it to set the jug down on the bottom stair. The four lamps that the program now drilled under all day were standing at the corners of the painted crosses where the porters had left them, cold.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-20.md:125:Cael did not write anything about it in words. On the back of his schedule, under the table, he wrote two numbers one above the other, *44* and *54*, the day the Archmarshal had been told the seat was full and the day the best practitioner alive had been laid on a pile. Karis saw them, and looked at him, and nodded once, and went back to her papers.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-20.md:143:What Jent had already given away, Cael could read without looking back at his own notes, because the house's counsel had been keeping score of it in the margin of her privileged minute, where he could see it. Three headings stood there in her small capitals, written before the sitting began. *EXECUTION. PROVISION. RECORD.* Through each of them now ran a single neat line. She had drawn the first in Jent's first minute, when he told the hood the petition had never said the enrollment was wrongly made. The second, a little after, when he called the clause law and took the house's history of it for his own, word for word. The third when he said again, for the minute, that he had never read a better-kept record of an enrollment, and the clerk looked up to ask if that was to go in as spoken, and Jent said, "Every word. I'd decline to soften it if I were asked," and something along the front benches shifted.
