editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-44.md:57:At Cael's left the counsel's pen moved. She had her privileged minute open in front of her, and across the top of the page, in her small capitals, written before any of them sat down, stood three headings. *RENEWALS. NINE DAYS. EVALUATOR.* She drew a line through the first.
