editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-01.md:89:It had come to him in the fourth exchange of the hardest bout of his life, in front of eight thousand people, out of the hands of a Gold who had begun the fight herself, and who had looked at him afterward on the stone as if he had asked her a question nobody had ever asked her before. The notice that came after it was the first that had ever said *Gold*. It was also the first that had ever warned him that what it gave him might not hold. *Stability: provisional — architecture under load.* The notice had found him on one knee on the stone, with a healer's fingers in his hand and eight thousand people looking down, and he had read it through twice there, before anybody strapped him. He had felt its words every day since.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-59.md:327:Seln sat down. He did it without any warning; he sat on the bank beside the track, with the satchel in his lap, like a man who has been standing at a counter for a very long time, and he put both his hands flat on the leather.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-29.md:89:The witness is a location. He had always heard that as a warning: a man who has seen a thing is only a place where the thing can be found, so do not be found. Now, in the empty wing, it sounded like a choice. He would rather be the place the boy could find.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-39.md:125:"That was the old way," she said. "Before the policy. An assessor who met a reading that went across many families could write that, pending further study, and the person went on with his life under that word, and nobody corrected anything. It was a door the old system left open. And the first three memoranda shut it, in order. Each of them cites an article of the directive by its number, the same directive I sat over at Halcenvane." She counted on her fingers, slowly, one, two, three. "The first: *close the door.* No assessor may designate by judgment of what a person shows; a station enters what the reading gives, and only that. The second: *remove the exit.* The provisional custom, pending further study, is struck; there is to be no designation that waits on study. The third: *delete the name.* The old word is discontinued, and every person who carried it is to be re-entered under a flag."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-38.md:213:Karis drew one more line on her sheet, under the five, and wrote beside it in small letters *for now, and provisionally*. She closed the enrollment book very gently, so as not to crack its spine, and put it on the corner of the table by the door, where she would see it at the second bell.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-40.md:35:"He is already theirs," he said. "Norhold was a knock, dressed as a kindness. A lent room, no paper, a warning that made you trust him. That is the third grade done well. And the case goes to the people it was taken from, by the hand of the one man you would have given it to."

